Drop the LLVM defines musl does not satisfy.

The Bazel overlay hard-codes what a configure run would otherwise probe for,
and the answers it hard-codes are glibc's. Three of them are wrong here.

HAVE_MALLINFO: mallinfo is a glibc extension and musl has neither it nor
mallinfo2, so llvm/lib/Support/Unix/Process.inc stops with

    error: aggregate 'llvm::sys::Process::GetMallocUsage()::mallinfo mi' has
    incomplete type and cannot be defined

HAVE_BACKTRACE and BACKTRACE_HEADER=<execinfo.h>: backtrace() and that header
are also glibc's. LLVM uses them only to print a stack trace when it crashes,
and it already has a path for platforms without them.

Everything else in the linux set is fine against musl -- getauxval, sbrk and
st_mtim.tv_nsec all exist.

--- a/utils/bazel/llvm-project-overlay/llvm/config.bzl
+++ b/utils/bazel/llvm-project-overlay/llvm/config.bzl
@@ -28,8 +28,6 @@
 
 posix_defines = [
     "LLVM_ON_UNIX=1",
-    "HAVE_BACKTRACE=1",
-    "BACKTRACE_HEADER=<execinfo.h>",
     r'LTDL_SHLIB_EXT=\".so\"',
     r'LLVM_PLUGIN_EXT=\".so\"',
     "LLVM_ENABLE_LLVM_EXPORT_ANNOTATIONS=1",
@@ -51,7 +49,6 @@
 linux_defines = posix_defines + [
     "_GNU_SOURCE",
     "HAVE_GETAUXVAL=1",
-    "HAVE_MALLINFO=1",
     "HAVE_SBRK=1",
     "HAVE_STRUCT_STAT_ST_MTIM_TV_NSEC=1",
 ]
